## Frequently Asked Questions  

**What file formats are available?**  
Design.com provides vector files (EPS, SVG, PDF) for printing and high-resolution raster files (JPG, PNG) for digital use. Animated designs are available in GIF and video formats.  

**Can I use my designs commercially?**  
Yes, all designs created with Design.com are yours to use for personal or commercial purposes.  

**Do I need design experience?**  
No — our AI tools and templates are built for beginners as well as professionals.  

**How much does it cost?**  
You can create designs for free and download low-resolution previews. High-resolution files and print-ready downloads are available with paid plans.  

**Can I edit my designs?**  
Yes. All designs are fully customizable, including fonts, colors, layouts, and icons.  

**What’s the difference between AI tools and templates?**  
AI tools generate designs instantly based on a text prompt, while templates let you start with a pre-made design that you can customize. Both options are flexible and easy to use.  

**Does Design.com offer printing services?**  
Yes, you can order high-quality printed business cards, T-shirts, and other materials directly from Design.com after designing them online.  

**What is the refund policy?**  
Refunds may be available for print orders with quality issues. Digital downloads are non-refundable, but you can re-edit and re-download your designs at any time.  

